\fs18 \cf3 Ref: EyeNet \'97 Seed investor introduction\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs19 \cf4 Dear Investor,\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf5 EyeNet\cf4  is on-premises computer vision that turns ordinary cameras into vision nodes \'97 they detect, decide, and act on site. Video stays local by default. We are raising \cf5 $500K\cf4  burn floor, with \cf5 $1M\cf4  / \cf5 $2.5M\cf4  above that for speed. Same product and unit economics. Extra capital buys GTM and footprint \'97 not a rebuild.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sb200\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf5 WHERE EYENET BEGINS \'97 WHERE INCUMBENTS STOP\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf5 EyeNet Vision\cf4  has an aggressive business model: it begins where incumbents stop. Six wedges on one platform \'97 any camera, hardware-bound scale, no per-camera blockers, detect \uc0\u8594  decide \u8594  act. Incumbents lack that model.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li85\sa40\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs18 \cf5 \'95  Vision-adaptive intelligent signage \'97 \cf4 Locked players / per-screen SaaS stop short of any-camera playlist scale \'97 EyeNet switches age / gender / group in ms and proves impressions.\
\cf5 \'95  Home care / Virtual Ward \'97 \cf4 Vitals-only RPM and cloud vision stop short of a safety layer \'97 EyeNet turns fall / help-call / zone events into the clinical stack without shipping video.\
\cf5 \'95  Peace of mind at home \'97 and away \'97 \cf4 Cloud cams and guard contracts stop short for empty houses, cottages, and students living away \'97 EyeNet gives presence + unknown-person alerts, phone pings only, footage on premises.\
\cf5 \'95  Shipping and industrial fleets \'97 \cf4 Cloud VMS stops when the link drops \'97 EyeNet keeps who\'92s onboard / in zone local; Matrix syncs on thin links across ships and plants.\
\cf5 \'95  HR presence \'b7 night & perimeter \'97 \cf4 Badge sheets and per-camera seats stop short of coverage \'97 EyeNet checks people in to the ERP/CRM and runs vigilance without 1:1 headcount.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sb200\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs19 \cf5 WHY EYENET DISRUPTS THE MARKET\
\pard\pardeftab720\li85\sa40\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \'95  Product \'97 \cf4 Sovereignty + operational action vs. cloud storage, bandwidth, and recordings.\
\cf5 \'95  Cameras \'97 \cf4 Any IP / Wi\uc0\u8209 Fi / phone camera as a vision node on a ~16 GB PC vs. locked kits.\
\cf5 \'95  Licensing \'97 \cf4 No per-camera licenses vs. per-camera seats that tax scale.\
\cf5 \'95  Outcome \'97 \cf4 Detect \uc0\u8594  decide \u8594  act (mobile, email, webhooks, signage, gates, ERP/CRM) vs. passive VMS.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sb200\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf5 WHY INVEST\
\pard\pardeftab720\li85\sa40\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf5 1. Clear wedge \'97 \cf4 Incumbents sell cloud storage on locked hardware; EyeNet sells sovereignty and action on cameras buyers already have.\
\cf5 2. Product already ships \'97 \cf4 Five of six products beta-ready (Presence, Signage, Vradar, Gate, Matrix); Sentinel in active build. Capital buys selling what works.\
\cf5 3. Tight path to revenue \'97 \cf4 U.S. TAM bands $0.5\'961.5B B2C and $2\'964B B2B/Enterprise; plan share \uc0\u8594  $5\'9645M B2C and $20\'9680M enterprise. Path: ~$1M (2027) \u8594  ~$8M (2028) \u8594  ~$26M (2029).\
\cf5 4. Seed ladder, not a rewrite \'97 \cf4 Underwrite $500K ops first; $1M or $2.5M only accelerates the same motions. CAC, LTV, and payback hold across scenarios.\
\cf5 5. SaaS motions \'97 \cf4 B2C Light $20\'96$300/mo \'b7 B2B Starter/Pro $500\'96$3,000/mo \'b7 Enterprise $5,000+/mo \'97 partners already signed (TMA / Talos, NewGen).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sb200\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
